From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: B Honey <9922368+Mhsbrian@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:06:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 15/23] nvk: fall back to nouveau when the device is not on
 NVIDIA's kernel driver

The RM integration replaced nouveau in nvkmd_try_create_pdev_for_drm(), so
a build with the RM backend could no longer drive a GPU bound to nouveau.
The Googlebook image has to run either kernel driver on the same NVIDIA
GPU (ANAL-300: NVIDIA's driver by default, nouveau as the alternative),
and one NVK for both keeps a single Vulkan HAL in the vendor image.

nvkmd_rm_try_create_pdev() returns VK_ERROR_INCOMPATIBLE_DRIVER, before it
allocates anything, for every render node whose DRM driver is not
nvidia-drm, so try nouveau after it. Any other result, success or a real
failure on an nvidia-drm device, is returned as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/nvkmd.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/nvkmd.c b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/nvkmd.c
index cb06c52..5eaeaf1 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/nvkmd.c
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/nvkmd.c
@@ -89,7 +89,16 @@ nvkmd_try_create_pdev_for_drm(struct _drmDevice *drm_device,
                               enum nvk_debug debug_flags,
                               struct nvkmd_pdev **pdev_out)
 {
-   return nvkmd_rm_try_create_pdev(drm_device, log_obj,
+   /* NVIDIA's kernel driver (nvidia-drm render node) through the RM backend,
+    * else nouveau: the RM backend turns down every other device with
+    * VK_ERROR_INCOMPATIBLE_DRIVER before it allocates anything.
+    */
+   VkResult result = nvkmd_rm_try_create_pdev(drm_device, log_obj,
+                                              debug_flags, pdev_out);
+   if (result != VK_ERROR_INCOMPATIBLE_DRIVER)
+      return result;
+
+   return nvkmd_nouveau_try_create_pdev(drm_device, log_obj,
                                         debug_flags, pdev_out);
 }
 
